  "body": "Seen on mote (America/Los_Angeles) at origin/main 0f8c3d867 plus the gateway-key concurrency branch (no change to sessions), 2026-11-08 00:40 PST:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestGatewayModeStatsNameTheGatewaySessions (0.01s)\n    sessions_gateway_keys_test.go:62: gateway mode off, days=1: keys [] leave out the gateway's session\n```\n\nThe fixture's record is written at `time.Now().Add(-time.Hour)`, which in the first hour of a local day is yesterday, and `days=1` doesn't count it. At 00:54 it was still red locally (TZ=UTC and TZ=Asia/Shanghai green at the same moment). From 01:09 it passes, 10 of 10.\n\nA first try that clamped the record to local midnight was still red at 00:54, so `days=1`'s window isn't simply \"since local midnight\" (maybe it excludes the boundary, or counts from a different start). It wasn't kept. The fix should hold every clock the stats path reads, or write the record at a time inside whatever window `statsForGen(1)` uses.",
