   "body": "Fixed on [fix/5690-gateway-stats-virtual-midnight](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5690-gateway-stats-virtual-midnight), commit [1554065a](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/1554065af326bf6cfa4ad4dfa06200c560bfe069), based on upstream `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe HTTP statistics test now runs inside Go's `testing/synctest` bubble at local 00:30, writes its record at that same virtual time, and checks the clock stays fixed across all six days=0/7/1 and gateway-mode queries. It changes neither the global timezone nor production clocks. The calendar advance is virtual.\n\nRestoring the original minus-one-hour fixture inside that bubble makes the actual days=1 query fail; the fixed fixture passes under `-race` in UTC and Australia/Sydney. An independent gateway-window test verifies exact midnight is excluded and midnight plus one nanosecond is included at consecutive day boundaries; its boundary mutation fails as expected. Related vet/build and formatting checks pass. I independently reran the HTTP test and the named midnight-boundary test.\n\nFull-suite, browser and cross-platform runtime checks were not run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
